WEBVTT

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.380
Hey! Welcome back.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.590
I thought you'd be back before us.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.550
What are you doing?

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:32.760
Throwing an after-party.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.220
Not a review session?

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.190
Yeah, you could call it that.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:37.930
Go get changed.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.620
All that talk about sportsmanship...

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.550
In the end, they just play dirty.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.000
I know. I understand how you feel.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.170
Someone elbowed me as soon as we started.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.230
Someone pushed my back.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.490
It made me lose all desire to run.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.950
Everyone's desperate to secure a good position.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.440
If it's a race for the best time,

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.910
we should run one at a time
and then compare results.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.410
They can't do that.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:09.380
Kakeru, you don't get it, do you?

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.240
Huh?

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.340
These complaints.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.560
There was no one running near you.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.220
You were running alone.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.520
That's not true.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.670
I felt bad to be wearing
the same uniform as you.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.670
It was fantastic.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.910
You finished third in your first race.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.270
I heard lots of people asking,
"who was that?" after the race.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:34.150
Yeah. Everyone was talking
about you, especially the girls.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:37.220
Lucky. I wish I had the girls' attention.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.790
Kakeru.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.160
Good work.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.250
Yeah!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:21.970
How did we do?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.880
How were today's results?

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.220
What did you guys think?

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.330
He doesn't want to comment.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.850
It didn't go as well as I'd hoped.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.420
It was fun at first.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.940
But I couldn't get the right pace.

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.900
It really hurts when there
are winners and losers.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.080
Isn't our goal to achieve official records,

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.120
so we can run in the Hakone Ekiden qualifier?

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:48.120
Since none of us did, it was a crushing defeat.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.160
Huh? Didn't Kakeru and Haiji make it?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.800
You don't need to count them.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.380
We should. They're on the team.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.460
I didn't even beat my personal
record from practice.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.260
Races and practice are different.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:07.810
If anything, experiencing the
difference was a major achievement.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:12.220
We'll overcome that in 
our upcoming practices, and...

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.650
Running like this...

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.560
We will make it in time running like this?

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.220
Of course.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.470
In two weeks, we'll attend
the Kikui Uni track meet.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.370
We'll practice even harder to prepare for it.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.830
Even harder?!

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.690
We'll start on a new training
schedule tomorrow,

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.370
increasing both distance and speed.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.630
Can't we have tomorrow off?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.670
I agree. You need to cool down after a race.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.200
There's no need to rest an entire day.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.950
Long distance running is 
all about practicing every day.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.760
I don't mind starting right now.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.100
Right now?

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.290
I've been drinking.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.450
I'm saying we should be taking
today's results just that seriously.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.320
We're running at Hakone, aren't we?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.430
Hey, what's gotten into you?

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:09.750
Don't worry. We all intend to.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.730
Then what are we doing now?

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:12.950
A review session?

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.540
This is just a party, isn't it?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.880
I thought it was a review session.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.900
Me, too.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:20.880
You had too much to drink.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.790
I think this kind of thing is necessary, too.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.100
Yeah. After all, we're a team.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.900
We'll practice hard starting tomorrow.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.730
I'm telling you, we should take tomorrow off.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:32.140
I think it's supposed to rain.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.100
Your jeans do absorb a lot of water.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.600
Don't be ridiculous!

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.190
<b><i>Dangerous Character</i></b>

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:53.340
It's not that I don't understand how you feel.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.830
But I understand how they feel, too.

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:59.810
It takes courage to face something head on.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:04.220
That's something you should
have by the time you start.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.000
Sure, you do.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.670
It's amazing that you were
able to compete with Fujioka.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.270
You must've been incredible.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:14.970
Not at all.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:17.560
There was nothing I could
do during that final lap.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.350
There was nothing we could
do from our first lap.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.830
That's why we should be
taking this more seriously.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.670
Hey, Kakeru. What should I do?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.470
Huh?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:29.290
I'm too heavy.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.710
Should I shed some flesh or shed some bone?

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.040
Issues of build are—

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:34.830
They exist.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.520
You know that, don't you?

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.740
Running today reaffirmed something for me.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.670
My body's not suited to long distance.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.700
I ran every day,

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.700
but it was a close race between me
and King, who took some time off.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.550
Is that why you quit running?

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:57.890
In high school, yeah. My coach told me to quit.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.520
Oh, I don't resent him for it.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.860
If anything, I felt relieved then.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.530
But that means you were frustrated, right?

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.440
That's why you told me.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.840
It means you can't give it up.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.840
Maybe you're right.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:22.740
I was frustrated, but it's also
the reason I was happy, too.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.880
That feeling when you start...

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:31.590
I never thought I'd get to taste that again.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.470
Then you should keep running.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.270
Let's both give everything we have.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.570
Where's Kakeru?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.700
He went ahead without us.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.060
Seriously? So we're back to how we started?

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.030
He wants to run at his 
own pace starting today.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.340
Nico-chan Senpai said he wanted
to try running at his own pace

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.250
during morning practice, too.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.920
What? You sure he didn't just skip?

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:11.310
Kurahara!

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.730
Shut up!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:39.910
It sounds like this thing
is groaning! It's creepy!

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.970
But my legs...

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:43.870
My butt is cramping.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:46.450
You're gonna curse us!

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.090
You guys don't need to be here.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:52.280
Yeah, but we can't move anymore.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.100
Maybe we can take a bath tomorrow.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.320
Let's do that.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.740
Isn't that what you said yesterday?

00:08:58.740 --> 00:08:59.810
I found it.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.980
A treadmill?

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:02.810
Yes.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.850
Ugh, but it's expensive.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.650
Is <i>that</i> what you've been shopping for?

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.690
Yes. There must be a cheaper one somewhere...

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:15.680
Hurry it up. You should go to Yuki's room.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.840
He'd never let me in his room.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:22.290
You're right, especially
not if they went with you.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.230
Jota, right there.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.210
I'll try the same spot.

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:28.100
Oh, it's so good.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.380
That's gross!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.680
Why are you in such a bad mood?

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.980
Is it withdrawal?

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.790
Anyway, Prince, does this
mean you want to run now?

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:42.210
No, but he's been pestering us
to practice all the time.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:47.190
I'd like to at least be able
to read comics while I do.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.280
This mouse is so hard to use.

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.990
No, it's not a mouse!

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.390
What is this?!

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.160
What? Shut up already.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:00.260
This!

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.290
Yikes.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.070
It's so I wouldn't accidentally smoke.

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.790
It's just like Rikiishi!

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:05.940
Huh?

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.630
Are you a fan of Joe?

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:09.830
That's not what I was trying to do.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.360
What's Rikiishi?

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.250
You don't know, you idiots?

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:17.510
He's a boxer. Joe's first,
 and greatest, rival.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:22.090
In order to lose weight, he didn't allow
himself to drink a single drop of water.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:26.960
He's a legendary boxer who ultimately
died while standing in the ring.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.340
Whoa.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.790
That's it?!

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:32.580
What? Nico-chan Senpai, are you okay?

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:36.150
Don't die while standing
during the Hakone Ekiden.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.380
Don't say such ominous things.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.410
You've touched my heart.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.430
How?

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:42.820
I won't be beat!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.660
I'm gonna buy a treadmill!

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:47.660
Finally!

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.330
<b>Add to Cart</b>

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:51.330
The buy button is so far...

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.420
Go, go, Prince! Go, go, Prince!

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:00.950
Shut up! Go to the second floor!

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:03.010
Stay out of my room!

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:28.320
Our fixed-pace runs are twice as long.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.900
The build-up runs have increased a lot, too.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.500
I considered each of you individually.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:37.210
We'll increase the intensity
of practice in any way we can.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:41.540
Let's try it. I'm sure we can do it.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:42.350
Yeah.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.430
Hold on. Is that okay?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:48.060
Build-up runs are speed training, right?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:51.810
They're exhausting and hard on your legs.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:54.930
What?

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:56.860
Yuki, you finally feel like running?

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.020
No! I'm just worried about you guys!

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.320
I knew you cared.

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:04.030
If we injure ourselves, we'll have nothing.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.770
Yuki's right.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:11.660
Some of you will struggle with build-ups,

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:16.210
so I've incorporated interval runs, as well.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.240
What?! You're adding more?

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:20.210
Were you listening to what Yuki said?

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:22.630
Let's do it. We're wasting time.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.590
Let's split into two groups.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.880
You can do it. You've got this, Prince.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:39.670
I can do it?

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.780
What do you think I can do?

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.450
Run on the left!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.660
Ugh

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:53.390
Clear the path!

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:54.660
Okay...

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.220
What?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.730
Are you running tonight?

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.080
Are you going jogging tonight?

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.070
Oh, uh...

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:21.880
We're exhausted from practice today.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:26.620
Then, even though we've stepped up
practice, we won't have gained anything.

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:28.030
But...

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.150
We were jogging at night for other reasons.

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:35.040
The fan club, right?
Have you been gaining members?

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.290
Slowly.

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:40.790
But I'm too exhausted to recruit.

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.670
Kakeru, behind you!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.870
Hey, watch out!

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.530
Be careful.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:51.720
Practice lasts until we get home.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:55.740
Teacher says the field trip
lasts until we get home.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.360
You've got energy to spare.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.170
I'm really thinking about quitting today.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:06.440
Let's keep going. We shouldn't
quit what we've started.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.120
He sure is fast, isn't he?

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:16.750
Whoa!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.460
It's so hot!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.920
This is it! This feels great!

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:29.300
The bath is hell,

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:32.400
but the sauna is pretty bad, too.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:34.680
Don't forget to hydrate.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:41.870
I'm sure you know, but Nico-chan
Senpai's pushing himself too hard.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.830
Kakeru's egging him on.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:46.110
Egging him on?

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:49.270
He used to run track.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:53.650
Having a fast guy tell him he can do it
probably makes him feel like he can.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:55.240
I think it's dangerous.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.380
What's the hardest part about section 8?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.920
Too easy. The Yugyo-ji Temple Slope.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:05.690
Correct.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.460
Yeah!

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:08.180
What else? What else you got?

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.140
Oh, uh...

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.430
King seems to be doing well.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:15.100
When he mentioned the Ekiden
in his afternoon interview,

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.290
it was apparently received very well.

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.880
It's working for him.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:19.890
Thanks for the food.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:23.610
That was quick. 
Did you get enough to eat?

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.180
Sure I did.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:29.110
Food tastes better since I stopped smoking.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:39.900
It's important to let your muscles rest.

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:46.930
I'm fine. I got plenty of rest this past month.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.810
Lead the team with him.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:01.880
With him?

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:04.520
Aren't you going for Hakone?

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.690
Oh, right. Prince.

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:16.910
The twins told me you 
were looking for a treadmill.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.490
Yes.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.640
My family's got one they don't use.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.460
I'll have them ship it here.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:24.750
What?!

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.420
You should've said so sooner!

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.510
That's great, Prince.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:32.260
Is... Is such a miracle possible?!

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:35.410
They're keeping it in the shed.
They were going to throw it away.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.280
Oh, god!

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:38.220
What's wrong?

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:42.410
Nothing. When one door shuts, another opens.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:43.940
That's not quite right.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:45.900
Oh, God!

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:50.280
<b>Ogre Shipping</b>

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.530
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:58.240
My alphabetical order, my alphabetical order...

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.110
This is surprisingly new.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:01.330
And it's free?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.590
You got a great deal, Prince.

00:17:04.300 --> 00:17:06.070
Let's turn it on!

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:11.710
I-It's too fast! Slow it down!

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.190
I can't! I can't!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.510
Wow! I've never seen Prince move so much!

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:15.510
I can't do this!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.970
Wow! Oh, wow!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.700
What is that sound?

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.030
I'm going to the field.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.460
Damn it.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:35.360
You can do it!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.860
Keep it up!

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:40.990
Two weeks until the next meet, huh?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.120
How are you feeling?

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.860
What is this? An interview?

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:47.210
I'm getting into shape right now.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.870
14:50:02.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.080
That's crazy fast.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.300
Okay.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.630
Joji, don't give up! 
You can pass him!

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:59.440
Wait. Are you sure that's right?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:00.320
Huh?

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.430
50:02? I don't think that's possible.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.480
What? But...

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.230
That's the same as two weeks ago!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.650
It doesn't make sense!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:14.420
What's his problem?

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:15.530
Fine.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.740
I'll run it again. Time it correctly this time.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.660
Kakeru!

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.660
Keep to the schedule.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:23.620
And Hana's times are accurate.

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:27.120
Sorry.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.050
What?

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:44.540
You don't need to run at the next meet.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.700
Only the members who haven't
achieved official records will attend.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.810
Why?

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.270
Is it because my time hasn't improved?

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.130
In that case, it's better that I run.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.070
If I run, I can get back in shape.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.200
It's pointless.

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.440
You can't see yourself right now.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.350
Then where can I leave my record?

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:12.590
There's always more track meets.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:15.800
In the first place, we've
focused our aim on Hakone—

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:19.680
Are you telling me to waste an entire year?

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:24.930
It'll all be for nothing
if I don't leave a record.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.930
Are records everything?

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:27.930
What?

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:35.360
Is running for you all about speed
and abandoning those who fall behind?

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:38.980
We're competing.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:42.560
We're not even guaranteed to run
in the Hakone Ekiden qualifier.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:45.990
Matching their half-assed speed
won't make me any faster.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.650
No one here is running half-assed!

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:56.590
Why won't you try to acknowledge
that everyone's trying their best?

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.660
Is it because they're slower than you?

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:02.300
Is speed the only thing that matters to you?

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:05.100
Then there's no reason to run.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:08.030
Ride a bullet train. Ride a plane.

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.520
They're faster.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.750
Wake up, Kakeru.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.120
It's not enough to just chase speed.

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:18.700
It's... futile.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.130
What?

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.620
Are you guys fighting?

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.860
You weren't sleeping?

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:30.700
I got thirsty.

00:20:31.050 --> 00:20:32.410
Excuse me.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.830
Kakeru. We're not done talking.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:37.880
Prince.

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:45.280
If you're only able to achieve
the same time at the next meet,

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:49.850
will you quit the team?

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:52.560
What?

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:57.460
Please. For the team.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:43.030
Next time: "Mismatched Runners."

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:45.030
<b>Mismatched Runners</b>
